      ":question/id": "3917eb67-0842-555e-a94d-d812e96bb32d",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-8x+80y+24z &=112 \\\\ 7x-70y-21z &=-98 \\\\ 4x-40y-12z &=-56\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-8 & 80 & 24 & 112 \\\\ 7 & -70 & -21 & -98 \\\\ 4 & -40 & -12 & -56\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1:=(-\\frac{1}{8})R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -10 & -3 & -14 \\\\ 7 & -70 & -21 & -98 \\\\ 4 & -40 & -12 & -56\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(-7)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -10 & -3 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -40 & -12 & -56\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(-4)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -10 & -3 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n",
